==English==

===Etymology===
From Chinese Pidgin English.

===Interjection===
'''[[long]] [[time]] [[no]] [[see]]'''

# {{idiom}} I haven't seen you for a long time.
#: ''Dave!  '''Long time no see'''!  How has Boston been treating you?''

====Translations====
* Czech: [[dlouho jsme se neviděli]]
* Dutch: [[lang niet gezien]]
* German: [[lange nicht (mehr) gesehen]]
* Chinese: [[好久沒見]] / [[很久沒見]]
* Cantonese: [[好耐冇見]]
* Russian: [[давно не виделись]],[[сколько лет, сколько зим]]<!--How many years(summers),how many winters]]-->

